3. THE C LANGUAGE AND ITS LIBRARY
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   See implements the C programming language as standardised in ANSI X3.159-1989
   and ISO/IEC 9899:1990 ("C89"/"C90"), and its standard library. It was written
   from scratch. The standard headers under /usr/include in the studio were
   written for See from the interfaces the standard describes; they contain no
   code from any C library or compiler. The machine it simulates follows the
   conventions of 32-bit x86 Unix systems (the System V i386 calling convention
   and address layout) so that addresses and frames look the way they do there.


